import json,collections,csv
OUT=__import__('os').path.join(__import__('os').path.dirname(__import__('os').path.abspath(__file__)),'..','..')+'/'
R=json.load(open('reqs.json'))
PH=['PH-0','PH-1','PH-2a','PH-2b','PH-3a','PH-3b','PH-3c','PH-4a','PH-4b','PH-5','PH-6a','PH-6b','PH-7','PH-8','PH-9','PH-10a','PH-10b','PH-10c','PH-10d','PH-11a','PH-11b','PH-11c','PH-12','PH-13','PH-14','PH-15','-']
byfile=collections.OrderedDict()
for r in sorted(R,key=lambda r:(PH.index(r['phase']),r['id'])):
  for tid,(f,t,fx,ex) in zip(r['tids'],r['tests']):
    byfile.setdefault(f,[]).append((r['phase'],tid,r['id'],t,fx,ex,r['cond']))
tests=list(csv.DictReader(open(OUT+'tests.tsv'),delimiter='\t'))
lit=[t for t in tests if t['class']=='CODE-LITERAL']
th=collections.Counter(t['theme'] for t in lit)
files=collections.Counter(t['file:line'].split(':')[0] for t in lit)
L=['# 05 — TDD plan','',
'Every module below gets its failing tests **before** its code, in the phase order of `06-migration-plan.md`; a phase is done when its new tests are green together with the whole suite, `npm run check`, the BDD run (both locations) and the private-details guard. Test ids `T-nnn-k` belong to requirement `REQ-nnn` (`03-spec.md` §10).','',
'## 1. Red-green order','',
'1. Write the phase\'s tests (this file, filtered by phase) and its scenarios (`features/`, filtered by the phase\'s REQs); run them: they fail for the stated reason (not a syntax error).',
'2. Implement the smallest change in `src/engine/` (new folder) or the touched module until they pass.',
'3. Re-point the literal tests of the phase (§6) to the registered template; each follows its disposition in `tests.tsv` (unchanged, harness, rewrite, changed, deleted, misclassified; R3-019).',
'4. Run the full gate; commit (each commit goes live through commit.sh, so a phase that affects a consumer is split additive-then-removal, see 06).','',
'## 2. How tests supply definitions','',
'- Fixture folder `.agents/test/fixtures/team-behaviour/`: `team.json` is **not** copied: the helper `template(name)` reads `templates/team-behaviour/<name>` of the checkout, so the conformance suite always tests what is shipped. Static fixtures: `teams-v1.json` (flat map with `wip`), `workflows-v1.json` (today\'s shipped file as schema 1), `example-team-v1.json` (copy of the topology definition with private names replaced by generic ones), `wip-limits.json`, `backlog.scope` pairs, `legacy-items/*.md` (the 14 word cases of `statusOf`), `invalid/*.json` (the 40-entry corpus of REQ-012).',
'- Helper `defWith(base, patch)` applies a patch object `{ "dotted.path": value | DELETE }` to a deep copy; `homeWith({ teams, workflows, items })` builds a throwaway backlog home (bare origin, clone) with those files committed; `entry(overrides)` builds a team entry.',
'- Unit tests of the engine call `evaluate({ definition, entry, entries, item, request, actor, caller, session, home })` directly with in-memory objects; command tests run the CLI in a `fixture(t)` repository as today.','',
'### 2.1 The shared harness on schema 2 (R3-002, phase PH-2a and PH-3a)','',
'Most literal tests run through `.agents/test/shared-fixtures.js`. Its change is part of the plan, in two steps:','',
'- **PH-2a (CLI unchanged, suite green on 174c76d code):** (a) `neutralTeam` and the routing of `cli()` that sends a team step on an item without a team to `backlog team update <item> --team neutral` are deleted: a test of an item outside a team runs the ordinary command, a test of team behaviour binds the item first (173 routed step calls in 10 files: shared-handoff-e2e 95, shared-update 15, shared-team-work 14, shared-sync-db 14, shared-handoff-commands 12, features 10, shared-team-stages 5, shared-audit 4, shared-team-lead-pop 3, shared-foreign-deps 1); (b) `intoTeam(slug, opts, team, status)` becomes `seed(slug, {team, status, fields})`, which writes the item file directly in schema 2 words and commits it (state seeding is allowed; the steps under test still run through the CLI); the 56 `--status` calls on items without a team go; (c) every `TEAM_LEAD` (70 occurrences in 26 files) becomes the entry\'s lead (`teamLead()` at 174c76d prefers `TEAM_LEAD` but falls back to the entry lead, so removing the variable and writing the lead into the entry keeps the suite green); (d) the 65 lines in 24 files that write old front matter (`stage:`, `review_state:`, `status: pending|in_progress`) write schema 2 words.',
'- **PH-3a (the cutover commit):** `sharedBacklog` writes `teams.json` as `{"schema":"backlog-teams/2","teams":{t1,t2,t3,t9}}`, each `{"workflow":"team","people":{"lead":"lead"},"lists":{"members":["ann","bob"]},"review":[]}`, and registers `templates/team-behaviour/team.json` as `team` in `workflows.json`; `wip-limits.json` fixtures become entry `limits`.',
'- Every `team migrate` test sets `BACKLOG_HOME` to a throwaway home; the gate of PH-1 and PH-3b runs under `.agents/scripts/check-real-backlog-clean.mjs` (R3-023).','',
f'Dispositions of the {len(lit)} literal-asserting tests (column `disposition` of `tests.tsv`, computed by `tools/tests.py` from the test sources): '+', '.join(f'{k} {v}' for k,v in sorted(collections.Counter(t["disposition"] for t in lit).items()))+'.','',
'## 3. Placeholder values (the filler table, tested by T-903-1)','',
'| placeholder | value |','|---|---|',
'| `<item>`, `<slug>` | the item slug | ','| `<seq>` | the item number |','| `<status>` | the item status before the step |','| `<step>` | the step name |','| `<from>` | the effective from-words joined by ` or ` |','| `<who>` | the `by` role names joined by ` or ` |','| `<actor>`, `<agent>` | the actor (`<agent>` in instructions: the agent the answer is for) |','| `<caller>` | the caller (Q-04) |','| `<value>` | the step\'s flag value |','| `<team>` | the command team |','| `<item_team>` | the item\'s team |','| `<session_team>` | the session team (Q-04) |','| `<workflow>` | the definition name |','| `<holder>`, `<holder_or_nobody>`, `<holder_or_author>` | `claimed_by`; with `nobody` / `its author` when empty |','| `<claimed_at>`, `<refine_started>`, `<review_started>`, `<reviewed_at>` | the field values (`None` when absent, as today) |','| `<refiner>`, `<refiner_or_nobody>`, `<reviewer>`, `<reviewer_if_active>` | the field values; `nobody` when empty; reviewer only when the status is an active review word |','| `<lead>` | the entry lead |','| `<list>` | the condition\'s list (items, slugs, dependencies) joined by `; ` (dependencies) or `, ` (items) |','| `<belong>` | `belongs` for one name, `belong` for more |','| `<n>`, `<count>`, `<limit>`, `<need>`, `<have>` | numbers of the condition |','| `<missing>` | failing completeness names joined by `, ` |','| `<how>` | `texts.refine_how` filled |','| `<review_refs>` | the list joined by `, ` |','| `<stage>`, `<verdict>`, `<VERDICT>`, `<records_verdict>` | the stage; the verdict; upper case; the verdict\'s `records_verdict` |','| `<reviewers_text>`, `<reason_text>` | §5.1 |','| `<level>`, `<of>`, `<held>`, `<hint>`, `<limit_text>` | §5.1 (`<of>` = ` of <key>` for repository/branch/team/member levels, `<repository> branch <branch>` for branch) |','| `<dependents>`, `<dependent>`, `<edges>`, `<state>`, `<command>` | §5.1 close gate |','| `<flags>` | offending request parts as flags (`--claim`, `--note`) joined by `, ` |','| `<repository>`, `<branch>`, `<bound>`, `<cwd>` | the item\'s repository and branch; the session scope; the working directory |','| `<forced>` | ` (--force past the claim rule: <first sentence of the bypassed refusal>)` when `--force` bypassed a condition, else empty |','| `<teams>` | rule team names joined by ` or ` |','| `<argument>` | the missing argument name |','| `<id>`, `<where>` | a dependency id; `this backlog` or `the backlog repository` |','| `<note>`, `<summary>`, `<reason>`, `<comments>`, `<comments_line>` | arguments; `<comments_line>` with whitespace runs collapsed to one space |','| `<now>`, `<today>` | value sources |','| `<work_commit>` | the work commit after the step (HEAD when none) |','| `<first>`, `<repositories>` | foreign waits `<repository>#<seq> (<slug>, status <status>)` joined by `, `; `repository <r>` joined by ` and ` |','| `<seqs>` | item numbers joined by `, ` |','| `<claim_first>`, `<dod>`, `<refs_note>`, `<stale_hint>` | the instruction or refusal of that name filled, or empty when its condition does not hold |','| `<review_refusal>` | the text of the failing review condition |','| `<idle_reason>`, `<claim_refusal>` | `message the agents holding the blockers below, or the coordinator` / `tell the coordinator`; ` (<active_items text>)` or empty |','| `<actor_or_none>`, `<actor_or_nobody>` | the actor or `none` / `nobody` |','','Every other `<...>` in a text is printed literally (instructions to the reader).','',
'## 4. Tests per module (written before the code)','']
for f,ts in byfile.items():
  L+=[f'### `.agents/test/{f}`','','| phase | id | REQ | title | fixture | expected |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
  for ph,tid,rid,t,fx,ex,c in ts: L.append(f"| {ph} | {tid} | {rid}{' (CONDITIONAL '+c+')' if c else ''} | {t} | {fx} | {ex} |")
  L.append('')
L+=['Runner tests (PH-0, `.agents/test/features.test.js`): T-RUN-1 tags attach to the next scenario; T-RUN-2 an outline expands one scenario per row named by its id; T-RUN-3 a conditional scenario runs only when `features/answers.json` selects its option.','',
'## 5. Guard tests (`.agents/test/user-guard.test.js`)','',
'1. **No flow word in the code of the user commands.** Every string literal and every property name in `x.<word>` or `x[\'<word>\']` of `src/shared/**/*.js`, `src/help.js` and `src/main.js` is checked against the word list = every status, side status, stage, verdict, role and field name of `templates/team-behaviour/team.json` plus `team`, `lead`, `member`, `reviewer`, `refiner`; allow-list: the binding marker `team` in the port calls and the field names `owner`/`owned_since` of the codec (R1-013).',
'2. **Import graph.** No file under `src/shared/` imports from `src/team/`; from `src/engine/` only `binding.js`.',
'3. **No hook parameter.** No function of `src/shared/` declares a parameter, destructured option or variable named `team`, `seam`, `hooks` or `callbacks`, and no file imports `seam.js` (R1-001).',
'4. **Primitives only.** A module of `src/engine/` or `src/team/` imports from `src/shared/` only the primitives `frontmatter.js`, `index.js`, `store.js`, `sync.js`, `safety.js`, `text.js`, `args.js` (plus `src/storage.js`, `src/errors.js`), and never assigns to a property of an imported object (callback installation) (R1-001).',
'5. **No vocabulary in the engine.** Every string literal of `src/engine/` is a schema key or token, or is in the allow-list read from the §8 table (R1-013).',
'6. **No team file read outside the engine.** No `src/shared/` file contains `teams.json`, `workflows.json`, `wip-limits.json` or `backlog.scope`; `TEAM_LEAD`, `BACKLOG_REVIEW_STALE_SECONDS`, `BACKLOG_TEST_SELF` appear nowhere in `src/`.',
'7. **Mutation checks** (T-905-1, T-905-2): copies of `update.js` with `"in progress"` and with `team?.step(a)`, a copy of an engine module importing `../shared/update.js`, and a copy assigning `seam.x = f` each make the guard fail with the number of the check.','',
'## 6. Migration of the existing literal-asserting tests',
'',f'Before: {len(lit)} CODE-LITERAL titles (of {len(tests)}) in {len(files)} files (`tests.tsv`). No test is deleted without a replacement. Rule per theme:','',
'| theme | titles | old files | becomes |','|---|---|---|---|']
rule={'T-BINDING':'definition-driven binding tests (`engine-binding.test.js`) for allow/refuse per operation + the old files re-pointed to the template as conformance (texts verbatim)',
'T-CLAIM':'conformance over the template after the harness change of §2.1; assertions per disposition','T-DEPS':'conformance; plus `engine-conditions.test.js` dependency predicate cases',
'T-FILE':'`team-cli.test.js`/`workflow.test.js` cases rewritten for schema 2 (`team-validate-cli.test.js`); the shipped-file shape tests become template validity tests','T-HANDOFF':'conformance; record-format tests stay as DATA-INTEGRITY unit tests',
'T-LEGACY':'replaced by `team-migrate.test.js` word-table cases (same 14 cases as input/expected of the migration); readers no longer translate','T-USERCONV':'CONDITIONAL on Q-01: kept as they are for option C, rewritten to read the configuration for option A, replaced by "unknown word" tests for option B',
'T-QUEUE':'conformance (pop, plan); user `next`/`list` ordering cases follow Q-01','T-REFINE':'conformance; DoD detection cases become completeness rule cases','T-REVIEW':'conformance','T-ROLES':'conformance + `engine-roles.test.js`','T-SCOPE':'conformance + `engine-roles.test.js` scope cases','T-STATUS':'conformance for team words; user status cases follow Q-01','T-STEPS':'conformance','T-WIP':'conformance for team levels; the levels outside a team are rewritten to assert no limit (D-18)'}
for t in sorted(th): L.append(f"| {t} | {th[t]} | {', '.join(sorted({x['file:line'].split(':')[0] for x in lit if x['theme']==t}))} | {rule[t]}; dispositions: {', '.join(f'{k} {v}' for k,v in sorted(collections.Counter(x['disposition'] for x in lit if x['theme']==t).items()))} |")
newt=sum(len(r['tids']) for r in R)
dc=collections.Counter(t['disposition'] for t in lit)
L+=['',f'After: {len(lit)-dc["deleted"]-dc["misclassified"]} literal tests stay team literals (re-pointed per disposition), {dc["misclassified"]} leave the class (machinery or storage, unchanged), {dc["deleted"]} is deleted with its replacement named; plus {newt} new tests T-nnn-k (§4) and 3 runner tests. The conformance file `engine-conformance.test.js` holds the cross-reference (old title → template rows R01–R29 of `03-spec.md` §9) and fails when a row has no test.','',
'## 7. Conformance suite','',
'`engine-conformance.test.js` registers `templates/team-behaviour/team.json` as workflow `team` in a throwaway home and runs (a) the re-pointed literal tests through a shared setup, (b) one test per §9 row, (c) the text-coverage check (every refusal and instruction key of the template produced by at least one test). It runs once (not twice: no bridge, R3-021) and is part of `npm test` and of every phase gate from PH-4b on; the expected added gate time is about 30 % of the 266 s of today\'s suite (the 188+56 scenario ids run in two locations).','',
f'## 8. Counts','',f'- New tests: {newt} (T-ids) + 3 runner tests; new scenarios: {sum(len([x for x in r["sids"] if x]) for r in R)} ids (`04-bdd.md`).',f'- Literal tests: {len(lit)}; dispositions '+', '.join(f'{k} {v}' for k,v in sorted(dc.items()))+'.',f'- Conditional tests (become active when answered): {sum(len(r["tids"]) for r in R if r["cond"])}.']
open(OUT+'05-tdd-plan.md','w').write('\n'.join(L)+'\n'); print(newt,len(lit))
